{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>As the children of Esau did to me.</b> Some interpreters say it means with respect to 'you shall sell me food for money' — if so, what did they do with the inhabitants of Ar, who are Moabites? And Scripture says 'because they did not come out to meet you.' And they needed this interpretation because it says 'the king of Edom: you shall not pass through me.' In my opinion, it refers to the reason of 'by the way, by the way we will go, as the children of Esau did to me' — for they went around Mount Seir by the way, by the way. And likewise it is written 'you are passing through the territory of your brothers, the children of Esau, who dwell in Seir.' Only the king — that is, the king of Edom — did not let them pass through the road of his province, for from there the land of Canaan was nearby. And therefore they passed by Ar, for so it is written. And many say they did not come out to meet them; rather, Israel purchased from them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The bracketed quotation 'you shall sell me food for money' resolves א״‎כ as an abbreviation for אוכל בכסף תשבירני from v. 28; the witnesses differ on the exact reading of this abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:06.218910700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}